# Daily run — 2026-08-07

## Roll
- Company: Midjourney
- Subject: hedgehogs (animal — passes the subject rule)
- Slug: midjourney-for-hedgehogs
- Rerolls: 0 (first draw was fresh)

## Concept
- Product: Bramble — a generative image studio for nocturnal insectivores.
- Demo: render-queue console (prompt bar with snout-input toggle, 2x2 render grid with U/V buttons, queue sidebar with dusk countdown, GPU-weather widget).

## Design direction
- Style: Moonlit generative-atelier, aurora glass dark mode. Deliberately the first glass/gradient entry after seven consecutive flat print-chrome styles (catalog, sticker sheet, nautical chart, storefront, wine label, mil-spec console, marketplace) — it parodies actual AI-lab design, which fits an image-gen company.
- Palette: primary #B79CFF (moonbeam lilac), accent #A3C585 (moss green, telemetry only), bg #0F1220 (nocturnal indigo).
- Fonts: Fraunces (display) / Outfit (body) / Fira Code (telemetry).
- Anti-sameness: style, palette, and font pairing all disjoint from the last 7 entries. ui-ux-pro-max suggested Kinetic Brutalism + Inter/Inter; overridden because it neither fit the bit nor differentiated well.

## Images
- Allocation: demo is photo-shaped (the render grid is the product's output), so 3 demo renders + 1 testimonial headshot. Hero image skipped: typographic aurora hero whose grid reuses the demo assets. Two testimonial slots intentionally show "portrait queued" frames as part of the joke.
- render-leafpile.webp (800x800): 1 attempt, judge pass (dewy leaves, indigo/lilac night palette, no text).
- render-hedgerow.webp (800x800): 2 attempts — first API call failed with HTTP 503 (model overload, script retry also 503); second call succeeded. Judge pass (dusk indigo sky, moss/lilac tones, burrow gap).
- render-mossbed.webp (800x800): 1 attempt (script auto-retried an internal 503 and succeeded). Judge pass (lilac dew highlights on moss, nocturnal forest).
- headshot-beatrix.webp (320x320): 1 attempt, judge pass (deadpan corporate hedgehog on indigo backdrop, lilac rim light).
- API calls used: 5 of 10 (one burned by the failed 503 attempt).

## Warnings / near-misses
- Gemini image endpoint was intermittently returning 503 (high demand); one budget slot lost to it. No other issues.
- One roll only, so no near-collisions with history.

